# Proposed (milestone2.md, "The product of polynomials": bv_conv_k): the finish of the product of two
# BallVectors whose coefficients are those of conv_k: the radius of conv_radius when every coefficient
# written is finite (the mask of the convolution), the bound of dot for min(n_x, n_y) terms was
# given (the mask of bound_dot_k) and the radius is finite, with the flag true; otherwise the
# canonical NaN and the flag false, and the product is the whole space. norm_finish_1 under the and of
# the two masks (bv_conv.py).
kernel:        bv_conv_finish
input:         rz
input:         mask finite
input:         mask okg
output:        r
output:        mask flag
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   the outputs are those of norm_finish_1, after the and of two masks

q         = and(finite, okg)
(r, flag) = norm_finish_1(rz, q)
